    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (74.48) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) anchoring our lineup, both benefiting significantly from favorable matchups against Quantrill and Young. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** leverages a strong SP skill advantage (+19%) to overcome his dynamic platoon penalty, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** is our premier start, capitalizing on an ideal platoon matchup (+14%) and an aggressive spot in the order. Meanwhile, **Nasim Nunez** (68.81) earns a high-scoring nod today; despite batting 8th, his efficiency is buoyed by a massive +16% park factor and the pitching volatility of Young, making him a sneaky source of stolen base upside in a day where we must prioritize speed.\n\nStrategic adjustments for today include fading **Nolan Schanuel** (48.11), who was our most difficult bench decision. While **Nolan Schanuel** projects as a reliable floor option, he lacks the ceiling of **Coby Mayo** (57.96) or **Jackson Merrill** (53.56), both of whom offer more significant raw power or situational advantages. Risk management remains a priority: while the park factors in our hitters' favor are generally high, we must monitor the status of **Gunnar Henderson** (58.94) and **Coby Mayo**, as both face Griffin in a contest where the catcher\u2019s arm strength (1.89s) poses a minor drag on our stolen base targets. **Jackson Merrill** also draws a difficult matchup against Yamamoto; his score is suppressed by a -16% SP skill adjustment, making him a high-variance play that we will need to monitor closely as the game progresses.",
